-- Morwenna Pascoe, the harbourmaster: answers what is said near her about
-- the tide and the lighthouse. The sea has her call each turn of the tide
-- (sea.talk).

on heard speaker, words
  if speaker is the target then
    pass heard
  end if
  put lower(words) into said

  if said contains "tide" or said contains "causeway" then
    ask world to named "sea"
    if the high of the tide of it then
      put "The tide's in. Nobody crosses to the lighthouse till it ebbs." into reply
    else
      put "It's out now, but it turns quick here. Don't get caught on the far side." into reply
    end if
    tell mua to act the target, {verb: "say", text: reply}
  else if said contains "lighthouse" or said contains "keeper" or said contains "ezra" or said contains "lamp" then
    tell mua to act the target, {verb: "say", text: "Ezra Trethewey kept that light thirty years. He went out the night of the storm and hasn't come back, and it's been dark since. He kept a spare key to the lamp room in the shed at his cottage, up Hill Lane. Hollis minds the garden now."}
  end if
end heard
